<BaseLayout
  title={"The Menu at JIN — Sushi and Omakase"}
  description={"Explore 24 illustrated appetisers, main courses, desserts, and beverages at JIN in Downtown Dubai."}
  ogDescription={"Explore 24 illustrated appetisers, main courses, desserts, and beverages at JIN in Downtown Dubai."}
  canonicalPath={"/menu.html"}
  stylesheet={"/inner.css"}
  script={"/inner.js"}
  active={"menu"}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
<main id="main">
<section class="inner-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="inner-hero-media"><img src="/assets/omakase-hero.webp" alt="An arrangement of JIN omakase dishes on the counter" loading="eager" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" width="1600" height="1000"></div>
  <div class="inner-hero-scrim"></div>
  <div class="inner-hero-content"><p class="hero-meta">The menu · JIN</p><h1 id="page-title">A menu shaped <em>by the moment.</em></h1><p class="hero-copy">Explore a selection of dishes imagined for JIN. Each one begins with the ingredient and ends at the counter.</p><a class="hero-scroll" href="#story">Explore <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
  <p class="hero-page">The menu</p>
</section>
<section class="menu-intro section-space page-wrap" id="story"><div class="intro-grid"><h2 class="display-heading reveal">The detail is <em>in the dish.</em></h2><div class="intro-copy reveal reveal-delay"><p>From a delicate opening plate to a final cup of tea, the menu follows the balance of season, temperature, and texture.</p><p>These dishes and AED prices illustrate the direction of JIN. The final menu and pricing will be confirmed before opening.</p></div></div>
<nav class="menu-index reveal" aria-label="Menu categories"><a href="#appetisers">Appetisers</a><a href="#main-courses">Main courses</a><a href="#desserts">Desserts</a><a href="#beverages">Beverages</a></nav></section>
<section class="menu-category section-space page-wrap" id="appetisers" aria-labelledby="appetisers-title"><div class="category-head reveal"><h2 id="appetisers-title">Appetisers</h2><p>Bright, composed beginnings that introduce the season with clarity.</p></div><div class="menu-gallery">
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/scallop.webp" alt="Hokkaido scallop crudo with yuzu kosho, translucent radish, and young herbs on dark handmade ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Hokkaido Scallop</h3><span>AED 88</span></div><p>Chilled scallop, yuzu kosho, translucent radish, and young herbs.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/sashimi.webp" alt="Seasonal silver skin fish sashimi with grated radish and bright citrus on a charcoal ceramic plate" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Silver Fish Sashimi</h3><span>AED 92</span></div><p>A seasonal silver skin fish, sharpened with radish and bright acidity.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/fish-selection.webp" alt="Pristine yellowtail selected for hamachi tataki and displayed over crushed ice at the JIN counter" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Hamachi Tataki</h3><span>AED 84</span></div><p>Yellowtail, smoked ponzu, shaved daikon, and a clean finish of shiso oil.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/tuna-tartare.webp" alt="Bluefin tuna tartare with avocado, smoked soy, shiso, and crisp rice on black Japanese ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Bluefin Tuna Tartare</h3><span>AED 98</span></div><p>Hand-cut tuna, smoked soy, avocado, crisp rice, and fragrant young shiso.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/botan-ebi.webp" alt="Botan ebi sweet prawn appetizer with citrus gel, caviar, and edible flowers on ivory ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Botan Ebi</h3><span>AED 94</span></div><p>Sweet prawn, citrus gel, Oscietra caviar, and a measured touch of floral acidity.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/wagyu-tataki.webp" alt="Rosy wagyu beef tataki with ponzu, charred scallion, and grated daikon on dark artisan ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Wagyu Tataki</h3><span>AED 110</span></div><p>Lightly seared wagyu, aged ponzu, charred scallion, and grated daikon.</p></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="menu-category section-space page-wrap field-pale" id="main-courses" aria-labelledby="main-courses-title"><div class="category-head reveal"><h2 id="main-courses-title">Main courses</h2><p>Warm dishes and nigiri served at the point where texture and temperature align.</p></div><div class="menu-gallery">
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/kinmedai.webp" alt="Golden eye snapper kinmedai nigiri with a delicate sear, citrus, and nikiri on handmade ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Kinmedai Nigiri</h3><span>AED 78</span></div><p>Golden eye snapper, lightly seared, with a touch of citrus and nikiri.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/otoro-brush.webp" alt="Rich bluefin otoro nigiri receiving a final brush of nikiri at the JIN sushi counter" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Otoro Nigiri</h3><span>AED 105</span></div><p>Rich bluefin tuna, warm seasoned rice, and a final brush of nikiri.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/chawanmushi.webp" alt="Warm Japanese chawanmushi egg custard crowned with sea urchin in a handmade ceramic cup" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Uni Chawanmushi</h3><span>AED 96</span></div><p>Silken egg custard, sea urchin, and the delicate aroma of dashi.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/nigiri.webp" alt="Five-piece chef selection of seasonal nigiri presented on handcrafted ivory ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Chef’s Nigiri Selection</h3><span>AED 210</span></div><p>Five pieces selected at the counter and seasoned individually for balance.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/miso-black-cod.webp" alt="Caramelized miso black cod with pickled young ginger and seasonal greens on ivory ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Miso Black Cod</h3><span>AED 165</span></div><p>Marinated black cod, Kyoto miso glaze, pickled young ginger, and seasonal greens.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/wagyu-robata.webp" alt="A5 wagyu robata sliced medium rare with sansho jus and smoked aubergine on black ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>A5 Wagyu Robata</h3><span>AED 240</span></div><p>Charcoal-grilled A5 wagyu, sansho jus, smoked aubergine, and fresh wasabi.</p></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="menu-category section-space page-wrap" id="desserts" aria-labelledby="desserts-title"><div class="category-head reveal"><h2 id="desserts-title">Desserts</h2><p>Restrained finales with gentle sweetness, toasted notes, and clean texture.</p></div><div class="menu-gallery">
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/black-sesame.webp" alt="Black sesame ice cream with crisp rice wafer and seasonal berries on handmade ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Black Sesame Finale</h3><span>AED 64</span></div><p>Black sesame ice cream, crisp rice wafer, and seasonal berries.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/matcha-crepe.webp" alt="Layered matcha mille crêpe with roasted kinako and a delicate touch of gold leaf" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Matcha Mille Crêpe</h3><span>AED 68</span></div><p>Fine matcha crêpes, light mascarpone, roasted kinako, and gold leaf.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/yuzu-sorbet.webp" alt="Yuzu sorbet with citrus segments, shiso granita, and a fine sugar tuile on ivory ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Yuzu Sorbet</h3><span>AED 58</span></div><p>Bright yuzu sorbet, fresh citrus, shiso granita, and a fine sugar tuile.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/hojicha-panna-cotta.webp" alt="Hojicha roasted tea panna cotta with sesame praline and caramel on dark Japanese ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Hojicha Panna Cotta</h3><span>AED 66</span></div><p>Roasted tea panna cotta, sesame praline, caramel, and a single seasonal blossom.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/miso-caramel-mochi.webp" alt="Three miso caramel mochi dusted with toasted rice powder on handcrafted ivory ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Miso Caramel Mochi</h3><span>AED 62</span></div><p>Soft rice mochi, white miso caramel, toasted rice powder, and sea salt.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/japanese-cheesecake.webp" alt="Airy Japanese cheesecake with sudachi citrus curd and a white chocolate shard" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Sudachi Cheesecake</h3><span>AED 72</span></div><p>Feather-light Japanese cheesecake, sudachi curd, citrus zest, and white chocolate.</p></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="menu-category section-space page-wrap field-pale" id="beverages" aria-labelledby="beverages-title"><div class="category-head reveal"><h2 id="beverages-title">Beverages</h2><p>Japanese tea, coffee, mineral water, wine, and considered pairings for the meal.</p></div><div class="menu-gallery">
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/coffee.webp" alt="Single-origin Japanese pour-over coffee served in a hand-thrown ceramic cup beside its carafe" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Japanese Pour-over</h3><span>AED 38</span></div><p>A precise single-origin coffee with cocoa depth and a clean, floral finish.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/gyokuro-tea.webp" alt="Uji gyokuro green tea served from a low Japanese teapot into a dark ceramic cup" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Uji Gyokuro</h3><span>AED 48</span></div><p>Shade-grown green tea with deep umami, soft sweetness, and a long finish.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/mineral-water.webp" alt="Premium Japanese still mineral water poured from a clear bottle into a crystal tumbler" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Japanese Mineral Water</h3><span>AED 32</span></div><p>Soft still water selected for its quiet minerality and palate-cleansing texture.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/koshu-wine.webp" alt="Chilled Japanese Koshu white wine served in fine crystal glassware at the lacquer counter" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Koshu White Wine</h3><span>AED 95</span></div><p>A fragrant Japanese white wine with citrus lift and a precise mineral finish.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/sake-flight.webp" alt="Three premium Japanese sake pours in distinct hand-thrown ceramic cups with an unlabeled carafe" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Sake Discovery Flight</h3><span>AED 145</span></div><p>Three expressions chosen to move from fragrant and light to textured and deeply savoury.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/yuzu-spritz.webp" alt="Non-alcoholic yuzu and shiso spritz with clear ice and condensation in a crystal highball" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="1000"></figure><div class="dish-info"><div class="dish-title"><h3>Yuzu Shiso Spritz</h3><span>AED 46</span></div><p>Yuzu, white shiso, verjus, and sparkling water served as a bright alcohol-free pairing.</p></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="quote-band"><blockquote class="reveal">One piece, one moment, <em>perfectly timed.</em></blockquote><p class="reveal reveal-delay">The chef adjusts each course in response to the ingredient and the guest.</p></section>
<section class="section-space page-wrap field-pale"><div class="split-story"><figure class="split-media reveal parallax-media"><img src="/assets/nigiri.webp" alt="Three nigiri pieces on handmade ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"><figcaption>The counter selection</figcaption></figure><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-delay"><h2>The chef’s <em>selection.</em></h2><p>For the full expression of JIN, allow the evening to move through a composed omakase progression. The chef selects the sequence and serves each course when it is ready.</p><p>Pairing suggestions will draw from sake, tea, and non-alcoholic choices, with the final offering confirmed before opening.</p><a class="text-link" href="omakase.html">Discover omakase <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="next-page"><h2>Make it <em>your evening.</em></h2><a href="reservations.html">Plan a visit →</a></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
